From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AztecBot <tech@aztec-labs.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 10:55:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(protocol)!: derive the protocol nullifier from the tx
 request's salt and expose it to every private call

The init kernel now computes the protocol nullifier from (origin, chain_id, version, salt) rather than
from hash(tx_request), and the tx_request_salt field of PrivateCircuitPublicInputs, PrivateContextInputs
and PrivateTxConstantData becomes protocol_nullifier: the siloed protocol nullifier, identical on every
private call. The raw salt no longer reaches app circuits.

Client side: the PXE computes the protocol nullifier once per request and hands it to every frame (and
seeds the simulated note nonces with it); the TXE does the same; the stdlib mirrors and Noir conversions
are renamed; TxRequest gains computeProtocolNullifierValue() / computeProtocolNullifier(); and
computeProtocolNullifier(value) in stdlib/hash takes the unsiloed value. Accounts, auth witnesses and
wallets are unchanged.

